{
  "templateName": "de Demo — Services Agreement",
  "bodyHtml": "<article><h1>Services Agreement (Demonstration)</h1><p>This Services Agreement (the <strong>Agreement</strong>) is entered into as of <strong>{{EFFECTIVE_DATE}}</strong>, by and between <strong>{{CLIENT_LEGAL_NAME}}</strong>, referred to as the <strong>Client</strong>, and <strong>{{FIRM_LEGAL_NAME}}</strong>, referred to as the <strong>Firm</strong>. The parties wish to set out the principal terms that will govern a professional engagement between them. A definitive statement of work or master services agreement may supersede portions of this document when executed.</p><h2>1. Definitions</h2><p><strong>Confidential Information</strong> means non-public information disclosed by either party in connection with the engagement, whether oral, written, or electronic. <strong>Deliverables</strong> means work product identified in a statement of work or otherwise agreed in writing. <strong>Services</strong> means professional, advisory, or technical services performed by the Firm for the Client as described in this Agreement or in a written addendum.</p><h2>2. Scope of services</h2><p>The Firm will perform the Services in a professional and workmanlike manner consistent with generally accepted industry standards. Unless otherwise agreed in writing, the scope is limited to the matters described in written proposals, change requests, or statements of work exchanged between the parties. The Firm may rely on information supplied by the Client and will use reasonable efforts to identify material gaps or inconsistencies.</p><p><strong>Summary of fees and commercial model:</strong> {{FEE_SUMMARY}}</p><h2>3. Term</h2><p>This Agreement commences on the effective date stated above and continues until completion of the agreed Services, expiration or termination of any underlying master agreement, or earlier termination in accordance with this Agreement. Either party may propose an extension; extensions are effective only when documented in writing.</p><h2>4. Client responsibilities</h2><p>The Client will: (a) provide timely access to personnel, systems, records, and facilities reasonably required for the Services; (b) designate a primary point of contact with authority to make day-to-day decisions; (c) review and approve or provide feedback on Deliverables within a reasonable period stated in the applicable schedule; (d) ensure that its personnel follow reasonable security and confidentiality procedures communicated by the Firm; and (e) not use the Services or Deliverables in violation of applicable law.</p><h2>5. Firm responsibilities</h2><p>The Firm will: (a) assign qualified personnel to perform the Services; (b) keep the Client reasonably informed of material issues, risks, and dependencies; (c) document assumptions and limitations where appropriate; and (d) return or destroy Confidential Information upon request when no longer needed for the engagement, subject to standard archival and legal-hold exceptions.</p><h2>6. Fees, expenses, and invoicing</h2><p>Fees are as summarized above unless a separate schedule specifies fixed fees, milestones, or retainers. Unless otherwise stated, reasonable out-of-pocket expenses that the Client pre-approved in writing may be invoiced at cost. Invoices are due within the payment term stated on the invoice or, if none is stated, within thirty (30) days of receipt. Late amounts may accrue interest at the maximum rate permitted by applicable law.</p><h2>7. Confidentiality</h2><p>Each party will protect the other’s Confidential Information using the same degree of care it uses for its own similar information, but not less than reasonable care. Confidential Information may be disclosed to employees, contractors, and professional advisers who have a need to know and who are bound by confidentiality obligations no less protective than those in this Agreement. Required disclosures under law are permitted after reasonable notice to the other party where legally allowed.</p><h2>8. Intellectual property</h2><p>Unless a statement of work provides otherwise, the Firm retains ownership of pre-existing materials, tools, and methodologies. Upon full payment of applicable fees, the Client receives a non-exclusive license to use Deliverables for its internal business purposes, excluding resale or redistribution of the Firm’s underlying tools except as embedded in Deliverables.</p><h2>9. Limitation of liability (demonstration)</h2><p><strong>This section is for demonstration only.</strong> To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, except for a party’s indemnity obligations or willful misconduct, each party’s aggregate liability arising out of or related to this Agreement will not exceed the fees paid or payable by the Client to the Firm for the Services giving rise to the claim during the three (3) months preceding the claim. Neither party will be liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for loss of profits, revenue, goodwill, or data, even if advised of the possibility of such damages.</p><h2>10. Indemnity (outline)</h2><p>Each party will defend and indemnify the other against third-party claims arising from the indemnifying party’s gross negligence or willful misconduct, subject to prompt notice, reasonable cooperation, and sole control of the defense for the indemnifying party where applicable. The scope of indemnities in production agreements should be tailored by counsel.</p><h2>11. Governing law and dispute resolution</h2><p>This Agreement is governed by <strong>{{GOVERNING_LAW}}</strong>. The parties will attempt in good faith to resolve disputes through escalation between project sponsors before commencing formal proceedings, except where injunctive relief is necessary to protect Confidential Information or intellectual property.</p><h2>12. Notices</h2><p>Formal notices under this Agreement must be in writing and delivered to the addresses or email inboxes the parties designate from time to time. Operational communications may use email without constituting formal notice unless the sending party expressly marks a message as a formal notice under this Agreement.</p><h2>13. General</h2><p>This Agreement constitutes the entire understanding of the parties regarding its subject matter and supersedes prior oral or written communications that are inconsistent with it. If any provision is held invalid, the remainder remains enforceable. No waiver is effective unless in writing. The Client may not assign this Agreement without the Firm’s prior written consent except in connection with a merger or sale of substantially all assets, where notice is provided.</p><h2>14. Signatures</h2><p>The parties intend to execute this Agreement electronically or on paper. Electronic signatures captured through the Firm’s systems, when enabled, are intended to have the same effect as handwritten signatures to the extent permitted by law.</p><p><em>This is a demonstration template only. It is not legal advice, may not reflect your jurisdiction, and is not intended for external use without review by qualified counsel.</em></p></article>",
